---
description: Standards for Python cicd implementation
globs: ["**/*.py"]
alwaysApply: true
---
# Python CI/CD Standards

<rule>
name: python_cicd
description: Standards for Python continuous integration and deployment
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\.py$"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      ## Python CI/CD Best Practices

      ### Build Process
      1. Use standardized build tools:
         ```yaml
         # pyproject.toml
         [build-system]
         requires = ["setuptools>=45", "wheel"]
         build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"
         ```

      2. Define build steps clearly:
         ```yaml
         # GitHub Actions example
         name: Build Python Package
         on: [push]
         
         jobs:
           build:
             runs-on: ubuntu-latest
             steps:
             - uses: actions/checkout@v2
             - name: Set up Python
               uses: actions/setup-python@v2
             - name: Install dependencies
               run: |
                 python -m pip install --upgrade pip
                 pip install -r requirements.txt
             - name: Build package
               run: python -m build
         ```

      ### Automated Testing
      1. Run tests in CI pipeline:
         ```yaml
         - name: Run tests
           run: |
             pytest tests/
             coverage run -m pytest
             coverage report
         ```

      2. Include multiple test types:
         - Unit tests
         - Integration tests
         - End-to-end tests
         - Performance tests

      ### Code Quality Checks
      1. Implement linting and formatting:
         ```yaml
         - name: Lint code
           run: |
             flake8 .
             black --check .
             isort --check-only .
             mypy .
         ```

      2. Security scanning:
         ```yaml
         - name: Security scan
           run: |
             bandit -r .
             safety check
         ```

      ### Deployment Procedures
      1. Automated deployment steps:
         ```yaml
         deploy:
           needs: [build, test]
           runs-on: ubuntu-latest
           steps:
             - name: Deploy to production
               if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
               run: |
                 # Deploy steps here
         ```

      2. Environment-specific deployments:
         - Development
         - Staging
         - Production

      ### Version Management
      1. Semantic versioning:
         ```python
         # setup.cfg
         [metadata]
         version = attr: mypackage.__version__
         ```

      2. Automated version bumping:
         - Major: Breaking changes
         - Minor: New features
         - Patch: Bug fixes

      ### Best Practices
      1. Use feature flags for gradual rollout
      2. Implement blue-green deployments
      3. Automate rollback procedures
      4. Monitor deployment health
      5. Document deployment process

examples:
  - input: |
      # Bad: Manual deployment process
      ssh user@server
      git pull
      pip install -r requirements.txt
      systemctl restart app

      # Good: Automated deployment
      name: Deploy to Production
      on:
        push:
          branches: [main]
      
      jobs:
        deploy:
          runs-on: ubuntu-latest
          steps:
            - uses: actions/checkout@v2
            - name: Deploy
              uses: some-deploy-action@v1
              with:
                token: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_TOKEN }}
    output: "Deployment follows automation best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
  tags: ["python", "ci-cd", "deployment", "automation"]
</rule> 